# Every path has an owner, so nothing merges unreviewed by someone who knows it.
# One developer today: every line resolves to the same person. That is not pointless —
# it is the file that stops being a formality the day a second developer arrives, and
# GitHub will request the review automatically from then on.
#
# Enforcement note: "require review from Code Owners" is a branch-protection setting,
# and branch protection is not available on a PRIVATE repository on the GitHub Free
# plan. Until this repo is on Pro (or public), this file documents ownership and
# auto-requests review; it does not block a merge. See docs/implementation/03-github-workflow.md §3.

